# Build output and local state. Copying bin/ and obj/ into the build stage is
# the classic way to get a container that mysteriously runs yesterday's code:
# the host's artefacts land on top of the ones the image just built, and they
# were compiled for a different machine.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Secrets. .env is gitignored too, and the container reads its configuration
# from real environment variables — but the two protections are worth having
# separately, because a build context is not a git checkout.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not part of the image. The tests and the comparison scripts run against a
# live pair of APIs on a developer's machine; the container serves.
AutoPartsHub.Tests/
tools/
*.slnx

.git/
.gitignore
.github/
README.md
*.log
*.log.err
